      "cr": 1,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — The Unknown Assassin.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, generated from the article's own words. XP ledger: level 2, power rating 4 → CR 1 as a operative. Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>The Blade That History Cannot Name</strong> — Unknown — connected to 'the arrangement' if it existed</p><p>Status: Unknown — alive, dead, or something else depending on which theory you believe</p><p>Someone killed Princess Peach on Highsun 1, 955 BF. That person's identity remains the central mystery of the assassination—the question that eighty-five years of investigation, propaganda, and civil war have failed to answer. The official narrative blamed Bowser, but the evidence is weak and Bowser has denied involvement consistently. Lady Bloomia's testimony claims the killer's identity is recorded in Princess Peach's list—'someone the Princess loved,' in the third column headed 'HELD THE BLADE.' If Bloomia exists and her testimony is accurate, she knows the answer. If she is fictional or fabricating, the mystery persists. Waluigi has encountered numerous theories about the assassin's identity. None are proven. All are disturbing in different ways. WAH.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Dagger</strong> — “The Blade That History Cannot Name”</li><li><strong>Sneak Attack</strong> — “That person's identity remains the central mystery of the assassination—the question that eighty-five years of investigation, propaganda, and civil war have failed to answer.”</li><li><strong>Keen Records</strong> — “Lady Bloomia's testimony (if authentic) describes this handprint as 'too large for a toad, too small for a koopa.”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/unknown_assassin</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/unknown_assassin</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
    },
